ears: Wilkes-Barre/Scranton's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.11\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.05 to +0.18), about +1.4\u00b0F since 1901. Wilkes-Barre/Scranton's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.15\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.08 to +0.23), about +1.9\u00b0F since 1901.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 5 of 12 months. Highs rose in 5 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Wilkes-Barre/Scranton's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.24 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 38.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 2018 (61.08 in); the driest, 1930 (26.12 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 3 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}